  1320	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
  1321	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
  1322	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
  1323	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
  1324	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
  1325	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
  1326	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
  1327	  stmap13, the same decision path also records exact-area guard statistics. In
  1328	  stmap14, the lower-moderate middle-slack relief must save two inverter areas
  1329	  instead of one. In stmap15, one-inverter relief is restored only after the
  1330	  mapper observes a high lower-moderate/middle-slack profile. In stmap16, the
  1331	  same behavior also reports each admitted relief choice. In stmap17, the
  1332	  adaptive one-inverter relief threshold also requires a material mapper-arrival
  1333	  improvement; arrival-neutral choices keep the stricter two-inverter fallback.
  1334	  In stmap18, the same decisions are preserved while near-miss rejected
  1335	  middle-slack candidates are logged. In stmap19, pre-profile one-inverter
  1336	  relief is seeded only by candidates with the same material arrival gain. In
  1337	  stmap20, the pre-profile seed is further limited to shallow nodes. In
  1338	  stmap21, deeper pre-profile seeds are allowed only with a much larger mapper
  1339	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
  1340	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
  1341	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
  1342	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
  1343	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
  1344	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
  1345	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
  1346	  the next slack band are admitted unless they match the high-reference,
  1347	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. In stmap28, that
  1348	  hard blocker is replaced by a soft area-margin penalty on high-reference
  1349	  moderate seeds whose slack and arrival-gain ratios resemble load-risky
  1350	  choices. In stmap29, the high-reference penalty is made continuous over the
  1351	  same seed band. In stmap30, the same load-risk surface is extended to
  1352	  high-reference strong deep seeds with a smaller continuous penalty. In
  1353	  stmap31, the strong-seed gain slope is damped to probe the penalty threshold.
  1354	  In stmap32, a cut-leaf load proxy adds a candidate-cut fanout-shape term to
  1355	  the strong-seed penalty. In stmap33, the cut-leaf term is normalized by the
  1356	  selected supergate fanout limit to test a library-derived drive/load signal.
  1357	  In stmap34, the drive-normalized term uses a bounded sublinear curve so high
  1358	  load/drive ratios do not automatically saturate the area margin. Stmap35
  1359	  preserves the stmap34 mapper decision surface and adds direct SCL
